# Test areas (docs/testing-flow.md "Areas"): the one place that says which part of the app a test, a source file and a
# unit-test file belong to. Read by CMakeLists.txt (a LABELS entry area_<name> on every ctest entry), tools/test/affected.py
# (changed files -> areas) and tests/test_main.cpp ([units]: SF_TEST_AREA runs only that area's TEST cases).
# First match wins inside a section, so list specific globs first. `*` matches anything, `/` included.
# A new test needs no line when a glob below covers it; one nothing covers fails `test_areas` (not the build).
#
# [areas]: name | what it owns
# [tests]: ctest name glob -> area       [units]: tests/test_*.cpp glob -> area      [paths]: repo path glob -> area
# [smoke]: ctest names of the cross-area set (start, open, stroke, save/load, one UI shot; under 3 minutes on CI)
# [core]: paths that mean the FULL suite when changed (headers half the app includes, build files). Besides these,
#         affected.py counts includers: a header included by 30+ files under src/ and tests/ is core too.

[areas]
sculpt | brush engine, strokes, masking, paint, textures, input devices, performance, hardware tiers
mesh   | mesh operations: remesh, cut, crease, levels, tube, parts, face groups, UV, retopo, forge spheres
cloth  | cloth, drape, garments
ui     | shell, panels, menus, shortcuts, gizmos, layout, scale, tour, library, support cards
render | viewport, camera, shading, environment, drivers
io     | file formats, projects, bridges (Blender, Maya), packs, plugins, export
ai     | AI generation, consent, links, network, updates, Discord presence
unit   | the sculptforge_tests shards: unit cases of every area (SF_TEST_AREA picks the cases; areas by [units])
site   | i18n, docs, guide, website, release and CI tooling, marks and other repo checks

